# Vauxhall Astra Mk1 five-door hatchback, 1980-1984.
#
# Vauxhall's first front-wheel-drive car and the beginning of the sales push that
# made it Britain's number two by the mid-1980s. Launched in the UK in March
# 1980, early cars from Bochum, with Ellesmere Port building from 16 November
# 1981. A rebadged Opel Kadett D, identical apart from badging and trim after
# Vauxhall's restyled variants were cancelled. Two-box hatch, saloon, estate and
# van; 1.2 OHV, 1.3 and 1.6 Family I/II, and the 1.8 GTE from 1983.
# https://www.aronline.co.uk/cars/vauxhall/astra/
# https://www.aronline.co.uk/facts-and-figures/unsung-heros/vauxhall-astra-1980/
#
# Dimensions: about 4,000 mm long, 1,640 mm wide, 1,380 mm high, wheelbase about
# 2,515 mm (Opel Kadett D figures; proportions checked against the photographs).
#
# Colours: Carmine Red, Astro Silver, White Gold and Helios Blue are documented
# Vauxhall colours on sale during the Mk1's life (Astro Silver 1978-90, White
# Gold 1978-87, Carmine Red 1980-87, Helios Blue 1982-88).
# https://www.bentasker.co.uk/images/Documentation/Vauxhall_Paint_Codes_-_Car_Touch_Up_Paint_-_Car_Paint.pdf
#
# Colour shares and weight: the Astra was Vauxhall's volume Golf-class car and a
# strong seller from launch, set at 260 against the Escort's 500 anchor: blue 85,
# red 65, silver 60, white 50. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 150 km/h: a game-balance figure for the 1.2-1.8 range (the GTE reached
# about 120 mph).
# Comfort 95/473: a 1980s small family hatch, below the Cavalier Mk2's 100/480
# and above the Escort; the line gives 322.5, rounded to 325.
#
# Dates describe road presence: launch March 1980 with a 12-14 year tail,
# staggered by colour.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-astra-mk1.blend in the blends repository.
# References: citycars/references/vauxhall-astra-mk1/ (gitignored).
# Image credits: 1983 Astra photographs via Wikimedia Commons (see reference file
# names for the photographers and licences).

obj=citycar
